e <base_ref> tickets/ tickets/closed/`) rather than reading the diff's add status. Found by redteam and probe.\n\nConfirmed correct: a ticket-only add claiming its own ticket is refused (tickets/ and tickets/closed/ both); a claim on a different ticket passes; file-and-close (fix.py plus the new ticket) passes; the call sits before close_tickets and any merge. tests/test_raid_land.py: 38 passed. The five new tests cover none of findings 1-3.\nunresolved_simplify_findings: not planned\n\nduration: duration: 2m49s\ntelemetry: wall=na agents=1 tokens=na cost~=$na\nseat: redteam \u00b7 runtime=codex \u00b7 family=openai \u00b7 route=gpt-6.1-sol \u00b7 model=openai/gpt-6.1-sol \u00b7 status: ran\nseat: probe \u00b7 runtime=claude-code \u00b7 family=anthropic \u00b7 route=self \u00b7 model=anthropic/claude-opus-5-5 \u00b7 status: ran\nraw-output: seat=redteam \u00b7 door=codex \u00b7 model=gpt-6.1-sol \u00b7 raw_id=20261109T212453Z-2445387\n"}

